#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:7
msgid "The agent stages scripts on disk and runs them via `-File`"
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:9
msgid ""
"As of [PR #230](https://github.com/yukimemi/kanade/pull/230) (agent version "
"0.42.0+), the agent:"
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:12
msgid ""
"Writes your script body to a temp `.ps1` under "
"`%ProgramData%\\Kanade\\agent-scripts\\<UUID>\\kanade-<UUID>.ps1` (Windows) "
"or `$TMPDIR/kanade-agent-<UUID>/kanade-<UUID>.ps1` (non-Windows dev only)."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:16
msgid ""
"Writes a _launcher_ `.ps1` next to it that sets UTF-8 console encoding then "
"`& '<your-script>' @args`."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:18
msgid ""
"Spawns `powershell -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "
"<launcher>`."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:21
msgid "This means your script:"
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:23
msgid ""
"**Can** have `[CmdletBinding()]` and `param(...)` at the top. The "
"call-operator boundary in the launcher gives your script its own scope where "
"those headers are valid."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:26
msgid ""
"**Should not** rely on `$PSCommandPath` matching the operator's source path "
"— it'll be the staged temp file."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:28
msgid "**Should not** write to `$PSScriptRoot` (see next section)."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:30
msgid ""
"Pre-0.42.0 agents used `powershell -Command \"<body>\"`, which parses the "
"body as a command-line expression and rejects `[CmdletBinding()]` as a "
"syntax error. If you see \"Unexpected token '\\[CmdletBinding()\\]'\" in "
"stderr, the host's agent is too old — upgrade it (see [agent "
"self-update](../operations/agent-mediated-updates/agent-self.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:37
msgid "`$PSScriptRoot` is read-only for `run_as: user`"
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:39
msgid ""
"When `run_as: user` (or `system_gui`), the child process runs as the "
"logged-in user — not as the LocalSystem agent that wrote the staged file. "
"The staging directory inherits its ACL from `%ProgramData%`, which grants "
"users **Read & Execute but not Modify**."
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:45
msgid "That means:"
msgstr ""

#: src\developing/writing-agent-scripts.md:57
msgid ""
"Write to `$env:TEMP`, `$env:LOCALAPPDATA`, or an absolute path under the "
"user's profile instead. Even for `run_as: system` (where SYSTEM can write to "
"its own staged dir), the directory is cleaned up when the script exits, so "
"writing siblings is fragile either way."
msgstr ""

